AB  - This study presents a visualization-based interactive interface for cultural heritage information exploration that overcomes the limitations of static, expert-centered museum search systems. By adopting ontology-informed data structures and database standards, the system visualizes contextual relationships in a three-dimensional heritage knowledge network and integrates generative AI to support both non-experts and semi-experts in autonomous exploration. From the National Museum of Korea's collection of 207,458 artifacts, 100 representative metadata combinations were extracted to implement visual feedback and related resource recommendations. This research proposes a new paradigm for cultural heritage information exploration through the integration of ontology-based structures and human-computer interaction principles, while suggesting possible extensions into mixed reality environments. © 2025 IEEE.
