AB  - As cultural traditions face disruption from generational gaps, climate change, and political conflicts, there is a growing need for new ways to engage younger learners in cultural preservation. Generative AI (Gen-AI) and immersive technologies offer promising tools, but little is known about how to design them effectively for cultural learning. My research explores how Gen-AI can support cultural revitalisation through interactive, emotionally resonant systems. I design and evaluate immersive learning experiences, such as voice-based storytelling and guided procedural tasks, using Gen-AI agents to personalise narratives and adapt to user input. Through user studies, I examine how these systems affect engagement, cultural reflection, and cognitive load. Looking ahead, my dissertation investigates how Gen-AI influences identity, bias, and social perception in cultural contexts. This work contributes design insights for building more inclusive, reflective, and culturally responsive AI systems. © 2025 Copyright is held by the owner/author(s). Publication rights licensed to ACM.
