AB  - This study evaluates the integration of Augmented Reality (AR) and Artificial Intelligence (AI), specifically through the use of a Generative Pre-training Transformer (GPT) for code generation in Web-based Augmented Reality (WebAR) applications. By leveraging ChatGPT for code creation, the research aims to ascertain the fidelity and execution efficiency of WebAR applications on web platforms. Employing a mixed methodology encompassing a bibliographic and documentary research, prototyping, and qualitative analysis, the study demonstrates that ChatGPT can successfully generate code for AR applications, ensuring accurate representation of specified attributes like colour, dimensions, and tracking capabilities. Despite its potential, the research highlights challenges such as the necessity for further empirical testing and exploration of complex project scenarios. The findings suggest promising avenues for future research, particularly in evaluating the comparative performance of AI-generated code and its implications for non-programmer application development. © 2024
