AB  - The widespread use of deep learning has ushered in a revolutionary age in the fields of drug development and pharmaceutical research. The many uses and consequences of deep learning in this area are briefly discussed in this abstract. Combining computing resources, large datasets, and cuttingedge algorithms has produced revolutionary progress. In this article, we look at how deep learning approaches have revolutionized the pharmaceutical and drug development industries. The development of new medicines has been hastened thanks to the use of deep learning methods. Potential drug candidates' potential of individualizing pharmacological therapies. There is promising potential for enhanced therapeutic outcomes with less undesirable effects using a tailored approach. Also, deep learning has rethought our understanding of how drugs and receptors work together. Computational modeling may be predicted with surprising accuracy by deep neural networks, which analyze large databases of chemical compounds and their interactions with biological targets. A constant goal is to find a middle ground where deep learning's computational power may coexist with more traditional types of biological understanding. Finally, deep learning may revolutionize the pharmaceutical sector and the drug-discovery process. Possible applications include accelerating the discovery of novel medications, enhancing the precision of individualized therapy, and shedding information on the nature of drug-receptor interactions.
