AB  - Drifting Pixels MR is an interactive mixed reality experience that frames the audience as a solitary space explorer embarking on a symbolic interstellar journey. Unlike traditional screen-based installations, this work leverages Mixed Reality to situate the narrative within the user's physical space, creating a heightened sense of "embodied solitude."The system features a generative narrative engine based on Jungian psychology, which analyzes user choices to map them to one of sixteen personalized "Earth Imprints"- symbolic artifacts rendered in a "white mold"aesthetic. This paper details the design philosophy, technical implementation, and narrative logic of the system. We contribute a semiotic taxonomy for space heritage and demonstrate how HCI can serve as a catalyst for existential reflection, mediating the tension between technological advancement and humanistic memory. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
