AB  - Traditional Business English (BE) textbooks are static, lacking personalization and failing to meet the dynamic demands of modern business scenarios such as cross-border e-commerce and international negotiations. This creates a significant gap between academic instruction and real-world professional requirements. This paper addresses this gap by presenting the design and implementation of a novel adaptive learning system for BE based on an AI-driven, multi-modal textbook architecture. We propose a "Human-Computer Collaborative"framework that integrates key AI technologies: Natural Language Processing (NLP) for dynamic case generation, Knowledge Graphs (KG) for content structuring, and Virtual/Augmented Reality (VR/AR) for immersive simulation. The system features an adaptive engine that personalizes learning paths and content difficulty based on real-time student performance analysis. We detail the system's four-layer architecture and the implementation of its core components, including a dynamic content generation module leveraging generative models like Deepseek and Qwen-QwQ-32B. The system's effectiveness was validated through a quasi-experimental study involving 88 university BE students. We conducted a comparative analysis between an experimental group (n=44) using the proposed system and a control group (n=44) using traditional textbooks. Evaluation focused on improvements in language proficiency, business skill application, and cross-cultural communicative competence. Results showed the experimental group demonstrated statistically significant improvements in business skill application (a 13.9% higher adjusted mean score, p <.001) and oral communication (p <.001) compared to the control group. Qualitative feedback confirmed high usability (SUS score = 88.5) and perceived professional relevance. The proposed AI-driven system provides a scalable and effective solution for modern BE education, successfully transitioning textbook design from an "experience-driven"to a "data-driven"model and offering a practical, validated pathway for intelligent higher education. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
