TI  - AI Empowerment, User Experience, and Cultural Translation: Design and Evaluation of a Cross-border E-commerce Platform for Cultural and Creative Products Targeting the Northeast Asian Market
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Virtual Reality and Interaction Design
SP  - 1157
EP  - 1161
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3820915.3821095
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3820915.3821095
AB  - Under the backdrop of the global digitalization of the cultural and creative industry and China's “Cultural Digitalization” strategy, the efficient international transformation of regional characteristic cultural and creative resources faces core challenges such as cultural discount, weak copyright protection, and fragmented user experience. This study takes the rich intangible cultural heritage resources of Liaoning Province (such as Xiuyan jade carving, Manchu embroidery, etc.) and the creative output of university art talents as objects, aiming to construct an AI-empowered “ArtLink Global” cross-border e-commerce platform for cultural and creative products targeting the Northeast Asian market. The platform innovatively integrates a generative AI cultural translation engine, a lightweight immersive display module, and a blockchain-based certification system, aiming to intelligently transform local cultural symbols into products that align with the aesthetic preferences of Japanese and Korean audiences, and provide a low-threshold, highly interactive cross-border transaction experience. This paper elaborates on the platform's three-layer architecture design of “Front-end Experience Layer - AI Empowerment Middle Platform - Resource Backend,” and demonstrates its technical implementation through a prototype system named “ArtLink Global” that integrates cultural translation, AR display, and intelligent customer service. A mixed-method approach (heuristic evaluation, user testing, A/B comparison) was used to conduct a preliminary evaluation of the prototype's usability and cultural adaptability. The results indicate that AI-driven cultural translation can effectively reduce cognitive bias by approximately 35%, and AR display increases user interaction time with products by about 50%. This study provides an integrated “technology-design-business” solution to the regional dilemma of “abundant resources but weak transformation,” and also offers a new paradigm for the application of AI and interdisciplinary approaches in the field of digital cultural heritage.
