AB  - We present HawkerVerse, a multisensory virtual reality (VR) system that supports immersive Singapore hawker cultural heritage experiences through embodied interaction. Using Newton Food Centre as a case study, we developed a system that integrates virtual architectural hawker environments, an Artificial Intelligence (AI)-driven conversational agent, and a haptic-olfactory interface to recreate the sensory and social dimensions of hawker life. Users can explore the virtual hawker centre via natural locomotion, converse with an AI agent powered by a local large language model (LLM), and experience realistic haptic and olfactory feedback related to representative hawker foods, such as laksa, prawn noodles, and Hainanese chicken rice. HawkerVerse demonstrates how multimodal feedback and context-aware AI can support interactive cultural learning and embodied heritage interaction in virtual environments. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
