AB  - We introduce PodaVR a virtual reality training system for cherry tree pruning. The application integrates a procedural generation engine based on parametric L-System grammars, specifically designed to follow the KGB pruning model. The system simulates interactive pruning scenarios with 3D representations of procedurally generated trees. The generative algorithm was evaluated in terms of completeness, frame rate performance, and generation time, confirming its feasibility for real-time immersive applications. Performance metrics were collected directly from Unity, including frame rate trends across different complexity levels. Results indicate stable system performance, with frame rates ranging between 60 and 130 FPS depending on the structural density of the tree models. The findings confirm that PodaVR provides a robust and efficient framework for integrating procedural modeling into immersive agricultural training environments. © 2025 IEEE.
