AB  - Virtual reality (VR) technology has fundamentally changed people's understanding of the production, viewing and dissemination of videos. It has also changed the original form of videos, providing people with a new method of visual stimulation and aesthetics. This project takes the Yanglai tower which tower in Banchangyu section of the Ming Great Wall as the research object and uses 3D sMax, Cinema4D and 3DsMax 3D models as platforms to explore immersive interactive virtual reality video and user experience. whith the aim of the virtual image interactive design method in the restoration and display of cultural relics, relevant design expressions were proposed based on the transmission of cultural relic information and the construction of spatial relationships.
