AB  - The making of augmented reality for mobile learning is a complex endeavor. The visual materials needed for such builds may be time-consuming to create given technological requirements. The emergence of artmaking generative AI (GAI) tools provides opportunities for to fast-track some of the work, in all phases: the design (research, brainstorming, color palette selection, visual elements, drafting, compositing, pilot testing, and others), the development (the creation of the various elements, alpha and beta testing), and the deployment (the release of the works into production). This chapter explores the work needed to co-create artworks with generative AIs, the visual editing required (right-sizing, color changes, outlining, formatting, and others), the accessibility design, the usability design, and other efforts to ensure effective augmented reality work for teaching and learning. Advances in GAI are also considered. © 2024 by IGI Global. All rights reserved.
