TI  - From Digital Reproduction to Cultural Symbiosis: A Pathway of Integration and Co-Creation in the Digitization of Cultural Artifacts
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Intelligent Engineering and Next-Gen Healthcare Systems (IEHNS)
SP  - 1
EP  - 6
DO  - 10.1109/IEHNS68708.2026.11607467
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047897641?origin=resultslist
AB  - The digitization of cultural artifacts has evolved from passive reproduction to active cultural symbiosis, yet rigorous quantitative evaluation of the underlying display systems remains insufficient. This study proposes and evaluates a technology-integrated digital artifact display framework combining Generative Adversarial Network (GAN)-based image restoration, photogrammetry-driven 3D modeling, and an immersive Virtual Reality (VR) presentation interface. An empirical experiment was conducted with 120 participants, assessing image quality using Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) and Structural Similarity Index (SSIM), and measuring user experience via a standardized questionnaire. The proposed GAN model achieved an average PSNR of 28.45 dB and SSIM of 0.89, outperforming bicubic interpolation by 18.0% and 18.7% respectively. User immersion scores increased by 35.5% and knowledge transfer improved by 42.1% compared to conventional 2D displays. These results confirm the feasibility and cultural communication value of the proposed system, offering a framework for digital heritage institutions. © 2026 IEEE.
