AB  - This comprehensive research reveals that artificial intelligence has achieved transformative breakthroughs in Chinese calligraphy analysis, with specialized multimodal systems like Calli Reader now outperforming human experts in recognition tasks while successfully quantifying traditional aesthetic theories into mathematical formulas for the first time. The field has advanced from basic computer vision to sophisticated deep learning architectures that achieve up to 95.6% character recognition accuracy and generative models that can simulate historical styles. These technologies are revolutionizing education through AI-powered evaluation, virtual reality (VR) systems that improve learning speed by 15–28%, and immersive metaverse platforms, thereby democratizing access to this ancient art form and enabling new methods for its preservation and appreciation. © ICST Institute for Computer Sciences, Social Informatics and Telecommunications Engineering 2026.
